# dialect-en-US.dict — THE VOCABULARY, AS DATA, IN ONE PLACE.
#
# Read by scripts/hooks/dialect-guard.sh. Nothing else in this engine carries a
# dialect word list; a second copy is how the last one drifted.
#
# FORMAT — one rule per line, TAB-separated:
#
#     <non-target form><TAB><target form>[<TAB>key=value[,key=value]...]
#
#   Options (third field, optional):
#     ext-exempt=css,scss   never flag inside files with these extensions.
#                           Reserved for words that are ALSO a legitimate
#                           technical value in that file type.
#
# FULL FORMS, NOT STEMS — DELIBERATE, AND THE REASON IS ARITHMETIC RATHER THAN
# TASTE. A stem-plus-suffix matcher is shorter and wrong in both directions:
#   * `analys` + `is` produces `analyzis` for the word **analysis**, which is
#     already correct American English;
#   * `catalogu` + `e` produces `cataloge` unless the matcher also learns silent
#     -e elision, i.e. English morphology, inside a hook.
# A couple of hundred explicit lines are auditable by anyone in a minute. A
# morphology engine is not, and the failure mode of a wrong suggestion is an
# engineer who stops believing the guard.
#
# ABSENT ON PURPOSE — the near misses, written down so nobody "completes" this
# list later:
#   dialogue    standard in American English too; only the UI widget is `dialog`
#   practice    the NOUN is `practice` in both dialects; only the VERB differs
#   analysis / analyses      already American; `analyses` is ALSO the British
#                            verb form, and the ambiguity is unresolvable from
#                            one word, so it is left alone
#   cancellation             American English keeps the double L here
#   enrolled / enrollment / controlled / patrolled     already the American
#                            forms; `enrolment` (one L) is the British one and
#                            IS below. Called out because the record started
#                            using this word on 2026-08-31 and "fixing"
#                            `enrollment` would be the guard causing the defect
#   analyzed / organized / any -ize form  already the target; a dictionary of
#                            NON-target forms never contains its own answers
#   advertise / exercise / supervise / revise / surprise / compromise /
#   franchise / improvise / devise / merchandise / televise / disguise
#                            -ise in BOTH dialects; not -ize words at all
#   metre / litre / fibre    real, and deliberately out of scope: this list
#                            covers words this record has actually produced,
#                            not the whole dialect
#
# Case is handled by the matcher, not by this file: every entry is lowercase,
# matched case-insensitively, and the suggestion is re-cased to the form that
# was actually written (lower / Capitalized / UPPER).

